[
  {
    "comment": "The P1-BEEHIVE treatment applied to Clayworks greenware. Only the dry states are stamped: every *-wet entry fires to shards, and a shard has no ware tier. Note that Clayworks does NOT displace vanilla ware for blue/red/fire clay \u2014 its `-natural` set is a wet stage that dries into game:<ware>-{color}-raw and goes on through the vanilla pipeline, so those three colours are already covered by ware-beehive.json. What this file adds is the six Clayworks-exclusive colours (azure, crimson, green, orange, pink, snow), which are the only ware that actually reaches a clayworks:-domain fired block.",
    "file": "clayworks:blocktypes/clay/raw/barrellid-raw.json",
    "op": "addmerge",
    "path": "/attributesByType/*-naturalfire-dry/beehivekiln/0/attributes",
    "value": {
      "rudimentsware": "stoneware"
    },
    "dependsOn": [
      {
        "modid": "clayworks"
      }
